hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7261","7308 Bishr bin Hilal informed us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to raid Umm Sulaim and the Ansar women with her, giving water to drink and treating the wounded.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7262","7309 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, he said: Sulayman told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Atiq, Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Atiq, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “There is a cure in the breaking of the fast, and it is the antidote to the beginning of the morning.” In the hadith of Ishaq: On an empty stomach, the wording is for Ali."
"7263","7310 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri said, “A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My brother has been complaining about his stomach, so he said: Give him honey to drink. So he gave him something to drink, and he said: I I gave him water to drink, but it only increased his speech, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has told the truth, and your brother’s stomach has lied.” And he said: Muhammad bin Ja`far, he said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with a similar example: He gave him drink, And he was healed (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7264","7311 Ubaid Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, loved sweets and honey.”"
"7265","7312 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Amr bin Harith, and Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, saying: Jarir told us, and Amr bin Ubaid, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, and Ali bin Hajar told us, He said: Shuaib bin Safwan reported, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Amr bin Harith, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Truffles are a form of manna, and their water is a cure for the eyes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7266","7313 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Ayoub al-Tai, on the authority of Qays bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, God has not sent down a disease except that He has sent down a cure for it, except for poisonous ones. So you should abstain from cow’s milk, for it destroys From every tree\""
7267"""
"7267","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, from 'Abd al-Rahman, who said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Allah has not sent down a disease except that He has sent down for it a cure. And you must use cow's milk, for it grazes on every kind of plant."""
"7268","7315 Zayd ibn Akhzam told us, he said: I am Abu Zayd, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Rukain ibn Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is healing in cow’s milk.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7269","7316 Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: I am Ishmael, he said: I am Praiseworthy, on the authority of Anas, he said: “Some people from Urina, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: If you had gone out to our side and were there and drunk from its milk And her urine. When they recovered, they went to the shepherd of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and killed him. They returned as infidels and sought food from the animal of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He sent for them, brought them, cut off their hands and feet, and gouged out their eyes."
"7270","7317 Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Khaled, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, narrated to us, he said: Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “People from ‘Urinah came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They invaded Medina, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: If you had come out to defend us, So you drank from its milk, he said: And Qatada said: And from its urine, so they went out to the shelter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when they recovered They disbelieved after their conversion to Islam, killed a believing shepherd of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and sought protection from the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And they went off to fight, and he sent for them and they confessed, so he cut off their hands and feet and gouged out their eyes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7271","7318 Bishr bin Al-Hakam informed us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, “People came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said to them: If you wish, I will send you to the camels of charity, so that you may drink of their milk and urine. They said: Yes. So he sent them out, and they drove the camels and killed the shepherd. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought them, cut off their hands and feet, and nailed them. “Their eyes.” And he said: Hushaym narrated. He said: Praiseworthy narrated, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7272","7319 Nusayr bin Al-Faraj told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The talbinah comforts the heart of the sick person and takes away some of the sadness.”"
"7273","7320 Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ismail bin Aliya told us, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would become ill, he would order soup to be made for them, then he would order them to drink some of it. He says: It cleanses the heart of the sick, and cleanses the heart of the sick, just as one of you cleans dirt from his face with water. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7274","7321 Ali bin Khashram informed us, saying: I am Isa, meaning Ibn Yunus, on the authority of Ayman bin Nabul, on the authority of Umm Kulthum, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one of his family fell ill, a spear would be placed on the fire and would not be removed until it hit one of its ends. \""
7275"""
"7275","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la informed us, saying: Al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard Ayman, who is Ibn Nabil al-Makki, saying: Fatimah narrated to me, from Umm Kulthum, from 'A'ishah, that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Upon you is the disliked but beneficial: al-talbinah (barley broth). By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, it washes the belly of one of you just as water washes dirt from the face."" She said: ""And the Prophet (ﷺ) used to, when one of his family fell ill, not cease having the pot on the fire until he seized one of two outcomes: either death or life."" Ruh said: ""Fatimah bint Abi Layth, Umm Kulthum bint 'Amr ibn Abi 'Aqrab."""
"7276","7323 Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad informed us, saying: Uthman told us, on the authority of Ayman ibn Nabul, on the authority of Fatima bint Abi Aqrab, on the authority of her maternal aunt, Umm Kulthum bint Amr bin Abi Aqrab, and she was Aisha’s companion, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was If one of his family or others is distressed, and it is said to him: He does not eat food, then he says: You should stick to what is hateful and beneficial: Talbinah. Give it a taste, by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, it washes the stomach of one of you just as one washes his face with water to cleanse dirt, she said. Aisha: And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was that if one of his family fell ill, the twine would not remain on the fire, until he came to One of its two sides, either it dies or it lives.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7277","7324 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Musa told us, he said: I am Hatim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amara, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Allah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three in which there is a cure for every disease, except for the poisonous: senna And the Sunnah. Muhammad said: And I forgot the third. They said: O Messenger of God, this is the Sunnah we have known. So what are the Sunnah? He said: If God had willed, they would have made it known to you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7278","7325 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “You should take this black seed, for in it there is a cure for every disease, except poison, and poison is death.”"
"7279","7326 Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “You should use the black seed, for in it there is a cure for every disease, except for poisoning. And poison: death."
"7280","7327 Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: I am Hibban, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Abdullah bin Tawus told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed cupping and gave the cupper his reward, and he begged.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7281","7328 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ The best treatment you can use is cupping and sea urticaria.”"
"7282","7329 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Humaid al-Taweel told us, he said: Anas was asked, “About earning money.” Cupping, he did not say permissible or forbidden. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had cupping. He said: And he said: The best thing you can treat with is cupping. And the sea costus, do not torment your children with insinuations.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7283","7330 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us a reading from him, and I hear, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Umm Qays bint Muhsin, who said: “I entered upon a son of mine with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I commented on it, and Harith said: It is an excuse for him, so he said: Why do you deceive your children with this relationship? Al-Hindi, for therein are seven diseases, of which are pleurisy that erupts from virginity, and gives birth from pleurisy.” And the word is for Qutaybah. Al-Harith said in his hadith: Then Al-Zuhri says: He coughs due to virginity, and gives birth due to pleurisy."
"7284","7331 Ibrahim bin Al-Mustamir told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahm told us, he said: Ismail bin Ja’far told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, “A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a son of hers. She had commented on him due to his impurity, and he was Blood was running from his nose, so he said: Woe to you, do not kill your children. For any woman whose child has this pain, let her be made lawful for him. India with water, then give it to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7285","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, he said: Mus’ab bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a boy who had been pinned, so he said: What is it? Do you kill your children? Dilute the Indian custard with water, then spit it out.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7286","7333 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Musa bin Abi Aisha told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “We addressed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during his illness. He said: Do not give birth to me. We said: Hating the sick. He took the medicine, and when he woke up, he said: “None of you will remain except Ludad, other than Al-Abbas, for he did not bear witness against you.”"
"7287","7334 Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Umm Qais bint Muhsin, who told him that she had brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a young son who had not yet reached the age of He was eating food, and she had commented on him because of the impurity, so she feared that the impurity might be on him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What is the cause? Do you indulge your children with these relationships? “You should adhere to this Indian oud, for there are seven cures in it, including: pleurisy.”"
"7288","7335 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Abdullah, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Arqam, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, describing oil and wars as “pleurisy.” Amr Ibn Ali told him, Khaled disagreed with him"
"7289","7336 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Maimun Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to describe pleasures of sexual pleasure as Indian aloes and oil.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7290","7337 Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Sulayman informed us, saying: I am Hushaym, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata’, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, He said: “There was a man with leprosy in the Thaqif delegation, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to him: ‘Come back, as we have pledged allegiance to you.’”"
"7291","7338 Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Abu Salamah told me On the authority of Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no infection, no mite, and no yellow blood.” A Bedouin said: What is the matter with camels? The sand is as if it were an antelope. The mangy camel comes and tests it all? He said: “Whoever is more hostile to the first"
"7292","7339 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no infection, no mite, and no yellowing.” Then the Bedouin said: What is the matter with the camels when they are in the sand? As if it were an antelope, and a mangy camel would mix with it and tempt it? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who was more hostile to the first?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7293","7340 Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, that Bukayr told him, that Asim bin Omar bin Qatada told him that Jabir bin Abdullah returned the masked man, then said: “I will not leave until you are cupped, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Indeed therein is a cure.”"
"7294","7341 Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Ziyad bin Saad told me, on the authority of Humaid Al-Tawil said: I heard a person saying: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: The best things used to treat them are cupping, and cups,” and he mentioned \excuse me\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7295","7342 Humayd bin Masada informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best of “You treated with it cupping and costus.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7296","7343 Hammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim informed us, saying: My father, on the authority of Dawud al-Tai, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Husayn bin Abi Al-Hurr, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: “A Bedouin from Banu Fazara entered the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and behold, a cupper He used cups that he had for centuries, then cut it with a blade and said: What is this, O Messenger of God? He said: This is the size, and it is the best treatment. people with it”"
"7297","7344 Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan informed us, he said: Al-Harith bin Atiya told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, and Muhammad bin Abd informed us Allah bin Al-Mubarak, he said: I am Abu Al-Walid, he said: I am Yazid bin Ibrahim, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr told us, on the authority of Jabir, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he performed cupping on his head, while he was in ihram, because of a cloak he had on him.” Al-Harith said: “From a cloak that was on his hip.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7298","7345 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, was cupped while in ihram on the back of the foot due to a bruise he had.”"
"7299","7346 Abu Dawud told us, he said: A lecturer told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He cupped his head in a state of deprivation from a headache he was having.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7300","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Aamim told us, he said: Thabit told us, he said: Hilal told us, he said: I asked Ikrimah about a fasting person using cupping, and he said: “ He disliked for him to weaken it, and it happened that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had cupping while in ihram from a meal he ate from a sheep that had fattened it. A woman from Khaybar, and he continued to complain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7301","7348 Ismail bin Masoud informed us, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that he heard Abu Al-Ahwas speaking, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “The people of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to ask him to iron out their friend, but he remained silent. Then they spoke to him, but he remained silent. He said: They flattened him, burned him, and he hated that."
"7302","7349 And Yaqoub bin Mahan informed us, on the authority of Hushaym, he said: Mansour informed us, and Yunus informed us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade ironing, so I was ironed, but we did not succeed, nor did we succeed.”"
"7303","7350 Ubayd Allah bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim told me, he said: I am Abdullah, he said: Saeed told us, he said: Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, on the authority of Suwayd bin Qais al-Tajibi, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Hudayj al-Tajibi, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If there is a cure in anything: then in “A cup of cup, or a drink of honey, or cauterization, and I do not like to be burned.”"
"7304","7351 Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus informed us, saying: Abther bin al-Qasim told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was captured, he made the people pass by the Prophet and the two prophets with them, and the Prophet And the two prophets were with them, and the Prophet and the two prophets had no one with them, until a great crowd passed by. I said: Who are these? It was said: Moses and his people. But raise your head and look, and behold, great darkness has blocked the horizon on one side, and on the other, and it is said: These are your nation. These are equal to seventy thousand of your nation who will enter Paradise without being called to account. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and they did not ask him, and he did not explain. To them, and they said: We are them, and some said: They are our children who were born in Islam, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and said: They are the ones who do not They cover themselves, they do not cover themselves, and they do not fly, but they put their trust in their Lord. Then Okasha bin Muhsin stood up and said: I am one of them, O Messenger. God? He said: Yes, then another man stood up and said: I am one of them, and he said: Okasha preceded you in it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7305","7352 Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: I am Al-Aqqar bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of his father, so he did not He memorized it, and he stayed after that, so I ordered Hassan, a servant of Quraysh, to ask him, and he told me that he had asked him, and he said: I heard my father. He says: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He who trusts in himself does not trust in himself and seeks out.”"
"7306","7353 Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, who said: Abaya bin Rifa’ah informed me, on the authority of his grandfather Rafi’ bin Khadij said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Fever comes from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water.”"
"7307","7354 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, saying: Khaled bin Al-Harith and Abdah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, it was read to him while I was hearing, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, He said: Malik told me, on the authority of Nafi’, and Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Al-Mu’tamir, and Muhammad bin Bishr, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Al-Harith said: On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The fever From the stench of Hell, cool it down with water.” Ibn Bishr said: Severe fever (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7308","7355 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik and Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading was read to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: I Malik, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of Fatima bint al-Mundhir, that Asma’ bint Abi Bakr, whenever she had intercourse with a woman, She had a fever, took water, sprinkled it on her pocket, and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “commanding us to cool it.” \with water\"""""
"7309","7356 Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Hani Baghdadi informed us of a cobbler, Abu Bakr Al-Athram. He said: Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad told us, he said: I am Hammad. On the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you has a fever, let him sprinkle cold water on him three times as a way to prevent magic.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7310","7357 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: I am Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Hudhayfah, on the authority of his paternal aunt. She said: I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there was a watering can hanging with water dripping on it for fever, so I said: “O Messenger of God, won’t you pray for May God reveal it to you? He said: The people who will be most afflicted are the prophets, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7311","7358 Al-Hasan bin Ishaq told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Abu Jamrah, he said: I used to keep the crowds away from Ibn Abbas, so I got up from him, and he said to me: Where were you? I said: Fever. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fever is from the breath of Hell, so cool it with Zamzam water.”"
"7312","7359 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Isa bin Yunus, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was bewitched. He was bewitched by a man from the Jews of Banu Zurayk, called Labid bin Al-Aasm, until two angels came to him one day. Or one night, he said: O Aisha, I felt that God had given me a fatwa regarding what you had asked for a fatwa. Two angels came to me, and one of them sat at my head, and the other sat at my side. My leg. One of them said: What is the man’s pain? The other said: He is healed. He said: Who treated him? He said: Labid bin Al-Aasm. He said: What about? He said: In a comb, a comb, and a palm tree, a male rose. He said: And where is he? He said: In Bir Dharwan, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to it. He greeted some of his companions and said: O Aisha, as if her water was infused with henna, and as if the heads of her palm trees were the heads of devils, so I said: O Messenger of God, did you not extract it? He said: God has protected me, and I hated to inflict evil on the Muslims from Him."
"7313","7360 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Malik said: And Al-Harith bin Miskin had a reading read to him, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, that he heard his father say: “Abu Sahl bin Hunaif ascended, and he took off his robe. It was on him, and Amer bin Rabi’ah was looking on, and Sahl was a white man, with good skin, and Amer said to him: I have not seen anything like today, nor A virgin, Sahl fell ill in his place, and his sickness became severe, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him that Sahl was unable to recover. To raise his head, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him, and Sahl informed him of what had happened to Amer, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “For what does one of you kill his brother? In the hadith of Al-Harith: Have you not been blessed? “The eye is right. He performed ablution.” Sahl went with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there was no problem with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7314","7361 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid and Al-Harith bin Miskin informed us of a reading of it and its pronunciation, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. On the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: “Amer ibn Rabi’ah passed by Sahl ibn Hunaif while he was bathing, and he said: I have never seen skin like today, nor any skin.” Hidden, then it was soon stumbled upon, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was told: Go easy. He said: Who are you accusing? They said: Aamer bin Rabi’ah said: If one of you kills his brother, if he sees something he likes, let him pray for blessings. Then he ordered him to perform ablution. Then he washed his face and hands up to the elbows and knees and inside his garment, so he ordered him to pour water over it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7315","7362 Ali bin Shuaib told us, he said: I am Maan, he said: Malik told us, and Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: I am Malik, On the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: “Amer ibn Rabi’ah saw Sahl ibn Hunaif taking a bath, and he said: By God, I have never seen anything like this today.” And there was no skin hidden, so Sahl took his place, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said to him: Do you want to see Sahl bin Hunaif? By God, he did not raise his head. He said: Do you accuse anyone against him? They said: We accuse Amer bin Rabi’ah. So he called the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Amer, and he became angry with him. He said: Why did one of you kill his brother? Did you not bless him? So Amer washed his face and hands for him. And his elbows, and his knees, and the ends of his feet, and the inside of his garment, in a cup. Then he poured water over him, and he went about with the people without any trouble.”"
"7316","7363 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Muslim bin Ibrahim, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Ibn Tawus told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The eye is a right, and if something precedes its destiny, the eye precedes it, so if “You have been washed, so wash.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7317","Ali bin Shuaib told us, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, and Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, and the pronunciation for it, he said: I Malik, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Zufar bin Sa’sa’ah bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. When he finished the morning prayer, he would say: Did I see one of you tonight and say: There will not be anyone left after me? “Prophecy, except good vision.”"
"7318","7365 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to admire beautiful visions, and he would say: Has any of you seen a vision? Perhaps the man saw it.” He sees a vision and is asked about him, and if he praises him well, it amazes him that he is a righteous man.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7319","7366 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Sulayman bin Suhaim told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad bin Abbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, removed the curtain while his head was tied while he was ill.” On which he died, he said: O God, have I conveyed the message three times, that nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophecy except the good vision that his or her servant will see. Indeed, I have been forbidden from reciting while bowing and prostrating, so when you kneel, pray venerately, and when you prostrate, strive hard to supplicate, for it is the Qur’an. that you may be answered.”"
"7320","7367 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: I am Malik, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A good vision from a righteous man is part of Forty-six parts of prophecy.”"
"7321","7368 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr told us, and he is Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Muslim’s vision is one of forty-six parts of prophecy.”"
"7322","7369 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “A good vision is one of seventy parts.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7323","7370 Ali bin Shuaib told us, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: I am Malik, On the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I heard Abu Qatada saying: And Ali said: And he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “The vision in the hadith of Al-Harith is good from God, and the dream is from Satan. If one of you sees something that he hates, let him vent it.” He should touch his left hand three times when he wakes up, and should seek refuge from its evil, for it will not harm him, God willing.”"
"7324","7371 Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, reading it, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Omar said, “Some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw Laylat al-Qadr in a dream during the last seven nights, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I see in your visions that they have colluded in the last seven days, so whoever is investigating them, let him investigate them in the last seven days. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7325","7372 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, Satan should not take my image.”"
"7326","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Uthman bin Omar told us, he said: I am Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Khuzaymah, on the authority of his uncle, my brother Khuzaymah, “He saw While the sleeper sees that he is prostrating on the forehead of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he mentioned that to him, so he lay down with him and said: Your vision is true. So he prostrated on his forehead.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7327","7374 Abu Dawud told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah bin Thabit, that his father, He said: “I saw in a dream that I was prostrating on the forehead of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he told him about that, and he said: “The spirit is to meet the spirit. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, bowed his head like this. Affan said: With his head behind him, so he placed his forehead on the forehead of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “Peace be upon him” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7328","7375 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abu Ja’far told me, he said: I heard Amara bin Uthman bin Hanif narrates, on the authority of Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that he saw in a dream that he was kissing the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. So that was mentioned to him, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, handed it to him and kissed his forehead. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7329","7376 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Bahdala, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’. On the authority of Kharshah bin Al-Hurr, he said: “I came to Medina and sat with the sheikh of the mosque of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a sheikh came and was leaning on A stick for him, and a man said: This man is from the people of Paradise, so he stood behind a pillar and prayed two rak’ahs, so I stood up to him, and when he finished his prayer, I said: To them: O these people, do you mean the people of Paradise? He said: Paradise belongs to God, and He admits it whom He wills, and I saw at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. A vision: I saw as if a man came to me and said: Go. So I went and he entered with me on a great path. While I was walking, he came up I have a path to my left, so I wanted to take it. He said: You are not one of its people. Then a path appeared to me to my right, so I took it until... I came to a slippery mountain, and he took my hand and took me in. I was at its peak, and there was an iron pillar with a gold tab at the top. So he took my hand and pulled me down until I took hold of the handle, and he said: Hold on to the handle. I told it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Good. As for the great path: it is the gathering place, and as for the path that turned to your left: it is the path of the people of Hell, and you are not of its people. As for the path that was presented to your right: it is the path of the people of Paradise, and as for the slippery mountain: it is the status of the martyrs, and as for the handle that “You hold on to it: it is the cloak of Islam, so hold on to it until you die, for I hope to be one of its people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7330","7377 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, saying: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Kharijah bin Zayd bin Thabit, on the authority of Umm Al-Ala. She was one of their wives, and she had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: Uthman bin Mad’un became our residence when The Ansar cast ballots regarding the residence of the immigrants, and he complained, so we nursed him until he died, then we put him in his clothes. She said: Then the Messenger of God entered upon him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So I said: May God’s mercy be upon you, Abu Al-Sa’ib. My testimony is that God has honored you. So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: How do you know? She said: I do not know, by God, O Messenger of God. He said: As for him, certainty has come to him, and I hope for the best for him. By God, I do not know and I Messenger of God, what will be done to me or to you? Umm al-Ala’ said: By God, I will not purify anyone after him. She said: And I showed Uthman a running spring in his sleep. So I mentioned that to him, and he said: That was his action. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7331","7378 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Saad, on the authority of Salih Ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “While I was sleeping, I saw myself on a block, so I removed from it what God wished. Then Ibn Abi Quhfafa removed sins or... Two sins and there is weakness in his removal, may God forgive him. Then it turned to the west, and I have never seen a genius among the people remove Omar’s tendency until he struck. \People are stinky\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7332","7379 Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Musa bin Uqba told me, Salim bin Abdullah said, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, “Regarding the vision of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them, he said: “I saw people They gathered, and Abu Bakr stood up and forgave one or two sins, but there was weakness in him, and God will forgive him. Then Ibn Al-Khattab, so it became impossible. West, and I have never seen a genius among the people smear his hair until he struck the people with a curse.” Then Hajjaj said: I said to Ibn Jurayj: What is impossible? He said: He returned, I said: What is a genius? He said: A hired worker"
"7333","7380 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Umar bin Al-Khattab, they said: What is your responsibility, O Messenger of God? He said: Knowledge. Mu’mar disagreed with him"
"7334","7381 Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “While I was sleeping, I saw a cup brought to me, and I drank from it until I saw irrigation running through my nails. Then I gave my favor to Omar bin Al-Khattab. They said: What is that, O Messenger of God? He said: Knowledge? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7335","7382 Muhammad bin Amir told us, he said: Mansour told us, he said: I am Al-Layth, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Al-Haad, on the authority of Abdul-Wahhab, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought on the night he was taken on a captivity to Ilya’, with two cups: wine and milk. He looked at them, then took the milk. Then Gabriel said to him: Praise be to God who has guided you to the right path. If you had taken alcohol, your nation would have gone astray. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7336","7383 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came May God bless him and grant him peace. A man left Uhud and said: I saw in a dream as if a canopy was oozing ghee and honey, and I saw people covering themselves with it. So the one who is independent and the one who is large, and I saw a cause reaching to the sky, you took hold of it and rose, then another act took hold of it after you, then he took hold of it. After it was another verb, then another took it after it, and it was interrupted, then it was connected to a verb. Abu Bakr said: Let me pass it, O Messenger of God. He said: Cross it. He said: As for the canopy: it is Islam, and as for what drips of ghee and honey: it is the Qur’an, its sweetness and softness, so the independent And the one who multiplies, and as for the cause that reaches the heaven: it is the one upon which you are the truth, you took it and rose, then after you another took it and did it. Then another act followed it, then another act followed it, and it was interrupted, and its act was continued. Was I correct, O Messenger of God, or did I make a mistake? He said: You were correct in some, and you were wrong in some. He said: Did you swear? He said: Do not swear. Muhammad Ibn Rafi’ informed us. He said: Abd al-Razzaq told us. He said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah. Sometimes he used to say: On the authority of Ibn Abbas, and sometimes he said: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he related the hadith when he gave his bounty to someone else. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7337","7384 Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My uncle told me, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar told me that he heard Abdullah bin Omar say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “While I was sleeping A cup was brought to me and I drank from it to the point that I could see irrigation running through my nails, so I gave my bounty to Omar. Those around him said: You have not explained that, O The Messenger of God said: “Knowledge”"
"7338","7385 Kathir bin Ubaid and Muhammad bin Sadaqa told us, saying: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Al-Musayyab, He heard Abu Hurairah say: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought on the night of his captivity with two cups of wine and milk, and he looked at them. Then he took the milk, and Gabriel said: You have been guided to the nature of nature, but if you had taken the wine, your nation would have gone astray.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7339","7386 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas bin Malik The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I saw tonight, as the sleeper sees, as if we were in the house of Uqba bin Rafi’, and we were brought with dates from Rutab Ibn Taab, so I interpreted: That elevation is ours in this world, and the reward is in the Hereafter, and that our religion has been good.”"
"7340","7387 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Al-Haad, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, On the authority of Salih ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunaif, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “While I was sleeping, I saw people being presented to me wearing shirts, some of which reached the size of the breast, and some of which reached the size of Other than that, Omar bin Al-Khattab passed by me with a shirt on, and we said: What did you explain it, O Messenger of God? He said: Religion? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7341","7388 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Abi Shuaib told us, he said: Al-Harith bin Umair told me, he said : Ayoub narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “He saw as if he had in his hand a piece of brocade, not pointing with it to anything of Paradise, except It flew to him, so I told it to Hafsa, so Hafsa told it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Indeed, Abdullah is a righteous man.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7342","7389 Ali bin Al-Hussein informed us, saying: Umayyah bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, consulted with the people on the day of Uhud, and he said: I saw, as the sleeper sees, as if I were wearing strong armor, and it was as if Cows to be slaughtered and sold, so I interpreted the shield to mean the city, and the cows to mean a group, and God is good. Even if you fought them on the highways, and the women shot them from above. The walls. They said: So they will enter upon us, a city that has never been entered upon us before, but we will go out to them. He said: What is your business then? He said: Then they regretted it. They said: We responded to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, his opinion. So they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, what is your opinion? He said: It is not for a prophet to wear clothing for his female slave and then put it on until he fights. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7343","7390 Abu Dawud told us, he said: Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am my father, on the authority of Salih, he said: Ubayd Allah said: I asked Ibn Abbas, Regarding the vision of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which he mentioned, Ibn Abbas said: It was mentioned to me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: While I was sleeping, I was shown that two gold bracelets were placed on my hands. I cut them off and hated them. He gave me permission, so I blew them and they flew off. So I interpreted them as: “They are liars who will emerge.” Ubayd Allah said: One of them: Al-Ansi, who was killed by Fayrouz in Yemen, and the other: Musaylimah."
"7344","7391 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Nafi told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Ibn Abi Hussein told me, on the authority of Nafi bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: Abu Hurairah told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “While I was sleeping, I saw in my hand Two bracelets of gold. I became concerned about them, so God inspired me in a dream to blow them. I blew them and they flew, so I interpreted them as liars. “They will come out after me.” One of them was Al-Ansi, the owner of Sana’a, and the other was Musaylimah, the owner of Al-Yamamah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7345","7392 Musa bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Burayd, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “I saw in a dream that I was migrating to a land where there were palm trees, so I thought it was Al-Yamamah or Hajar, and lo and behold, it was The city of Yathrib, and I saw in these visions that I shook a sword, and its chest was cut off. So, this is what happened to the believers on the day of Uhud. Then I shook it with another, and it returned to the best it had ever been, and behold, this is what God brought of conquest and the gathering of the believers, and I saw cows in it. And God is good. And when the group of believers were distressed on the day of Uhud, and when good, God has not brought us any good yet, and the reward for honesty that was \After the day of Badr\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7346","7393 Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Musa bin Uqba told me, on the authority of Salim, he told him, on the authority of A vision of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “I saw a black woman Frustrated, she left Medina until she came down to a place called Al-Juhfa. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, explained: The plague of the city has been transferred to Al-Juhfa.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7347","7394 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khabab, on the authority of Abu Saeed al-Khudri, He heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If one of you sees a vision and loves it, then it is from God, so let him thank God for it.” And let him speak of it, and if he sees anything other than that which he dislikes, then it is from Satan, so let him seek refuge in God from its evil, and not mention it. For anyone, it will not harm him.”"
"7348","7395 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ If one of you sees a vision that he dislikes, let him spit on his left three times, and seek refuge in God from Satan three times, and turn away from \The side that he was on\"""""
"7349","7396 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “A good dream is good news from God, and sadness is from Satan, and from a dream.” This is what a man tells himself. If one of you sees a vision that he hates, let him stand up and pray. I hate making mistakes when sleeping, and I like it. The restriction, for the restriction is stability in the religion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7350","7397 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Qatada On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The vision is from God, and the dream is from Satan. If one of you sees something that he hates, Let him blow on his left three times, and let him seek refuge in God from its evil, for it will not harm him.”"
"7351","7398 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ “If one of you dreams, he should not tell anyone about Satan playing with him in the dream.”"
"7352","7399 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that He said to a Bedouin who came to him and said: I dreamed that my head was cut off. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, rebuked him and said: “Do not inform of Satan’s manipulation of \dream\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7353","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'tamir narrated, saying: I heard 'Awf say: Abu Rajaa' narrated to us that Samurah narrated to them, saying: \The Messenger of Allah"
"7354","7401 I am Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman. He said: Abdullah bin Wahb narrated to us. He said: Malik told me, and another one before him mentioned, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Abu Al-Zinad told me, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred minus one. Whoever counts them will enter Paradise. A string that loves string.” The pronunciation is spring."
"7355","7402 Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Abdul-Aziz, he said: Abu Nadra told me, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri, “Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Shall I perform ruqyah for you, O Muhammad? He said yes. He said: In the name of God, I perform ruqyah for you of everything.” harm you, and from the evil of every soul and eye, in the name of God I perform ruqyah for you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7356","7403 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadhar bin Shumail told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, “that Some Bedouins used to bring meat to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: O Messenger of God, some Bedouin people bring us meat. We do not know whether they mentioned the name of God over it or not. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Mention the name of God and eat."
"7357","7404 Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Jundub bin Sufyan, who said: I witnessed the sacrifice of sacrifice with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the people in prayer, and when he finished the prayer, he saw sheep that had been slaughtered. He said: “Whoever slaughters before the prayer, Let him slaughter a sheep in its place, and whoever has not slaughtered, let him slaughter it in the name of God.”"
"7358","7405 Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id informed us, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Abdullah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, found Omar on a ride swearing by his father, and he said: God forbids you from swearing by your fathers, so whoever swears should swear. By God, or remain silent.”"
"7359","7406 Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Abdul-Aziz told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And when he entered the toilet, he said salaam, saying: I seek refuge in God from evil and evil things."
"7360","7407 Amr bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith, he said: My father told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, he said: Hanzalah bin Ali told me that Muhjan bin Adraa’ told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque, and behold, a man He finished his prayer while reciting the tashahhud, and said: “I ask you, O God, the One, the Eternal, the One who does not beget, nor is He begotten, and there is no equal to Him.” Uhud 0, that you forgive me my sins, for you are the Forgiving, the Merciful. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He has been forgiven.” Three times, Malik disagreed with him. Bin Mughal"
"7361","7408 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told me, he said: Malik told us, he said: Abdullah bin Buraidah told me, on the authority of His father, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man saying: Oh God, I ask you that I bear witness that you are God, there is no god but you.” The One, the One, the Eternal, and he said: You have asked God by His greatest name, by which He answers when called upon, and when asked by it He gives. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7362","7409 Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Abu Al-Zannad told us, Abd al-Rahman al-Araj told him, He mentioned that he heard Abu Hurairah narrating it, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “God Almighty said: Ibn Adam, and it was not appropriate for him to deny me, and the son of Adam insulted me, but it was not appropriate for him to insult me. As for his denial of me, it is his saying: He will not return me to the way He started me, and nothing is easier for me than the beginning of creation than for me to return it. As for cursing him, it is his saying: God has taken a son, and I am God. The One, the Eternal, the One whom I did not give birth to, nor was I begotten, and there is no one equal to me.”"
"7363","7410 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Suhail told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to bed, he would say: O God, Lord of the heavens, Lord of the earth, and Lord of Everything, separate love and intentions, the revelation of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Qur’an. We seek refuge in You from the evil of all evil. You take its corner. You are the first, so there is nothing before you. You are the last, so there is nothing after you. You are the Manifest, so there is nothing above you. You are the Inward, so there is nothing below you. “One thing, pay off my debt and free me from poverty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7364","7411 Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “She came Fatima, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked a servant, and he said to her: Who did you come to ask for who is more beloved to you or better than him? He said: So I calculated She asked Ali, and he said: Tell me: What is good? She said: What is good? He said: So say, O God, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Throne. Almighty, our Lord and Lord of all things, who sent down the Torah, the Gospel, the Criterion, and the Creator of love and intentions, I seek refuge in You from the evil of all things. Taking his forelock, you are the first, so there is nothing before you, and you are the last, so there is nothing after you, and you are the Manifest, so there is nothing above you, and you Inward, for there is nothing besides You. Pay off our debt and relieve us from poverty.”"
"7365","7412 Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Ja’far told us, on the authority of Al-Ja’ad Abu Uthman, he said: Abu Raja’ Al-Attardi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in what he narrates on the authority of his Lord, Blessed and Most High: “Indeed, your Lord is Merciful. Whoever intends to do a good deed but does not do it.” A good deed is recorded for him, and if he does it, it is recorded for him ten to seven hundred and many times as much. And whoever intends to do an evil and does not do it, “One good deed is recorded for him, but if he does it, it is recorded as one good deed, or God erases it, and no one perishes before God except one who perishes.”"
"7366","7413 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Bishr, he said: Mujma’ bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Mawhib, on the authority of Musa Ibn Talha, on the authority of his father, said: We said: “O Messenger of God, how can we pray for you?” He said: Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as you prayed for “Ibrahim and the family of Abraham, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham and the family of Abraham. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” Khaled disagreed with him. Ibn Salamah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7367","7414 Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Abu Hisham Al-Makhzoumi told us, he said: Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, he said: Uthman bin Hakim told us. He said: Khaled bin Salamah told us, he said: I heard Musa bin Talha, and Abdul Hamid asked him: How is the blessing upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I asked Zaid bin Kharijah Al-Ansari. He said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: “O Messenger of God, how is the prayer upon you?” He said: Pray for me, then say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed the family of Abraham, for You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7368","7415 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Hadi On the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, on the authority of Ali: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me these words, and commanded me that if any distress or It is difficult for me to say it: There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to Him, blessed be God, Lord of the Great Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7369","7416 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, and Abdullah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: Qatada narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He says when distressed: There is no god but God, the Great, the Forbearing, there is no god but God, Lord of the Great Throne, there is no god but God, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth. And Lord of the Noble Throne.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7370","7417 Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr told me, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id and Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of my father. Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to supplicate them during times of distress: There is no god but God, the Great, the Forbearing, there is no god but God, the Great, the Forbearing. There is no god but God, Lord of the seven heavens, and Lord of the Noble Throne.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7371","7418 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: Yahya, Abd al-Rahman, and Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Sa’d bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustawirad ibn Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, “He prayed next to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night. And he used to say in his bowing: Glory be to my Lord the Great, and in his prostration: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7372","7419 Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told us, he said: Khalaf bin Tamim told us, he said: Israel told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman. Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not teach you some words that if you say them, you will be forgiven, on the grounds that you are forgiven: There is no god but God, the Most High, the Great, there is no god but God, He is the Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to God, Lord of the Mighty Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds.” Ali bin Saleh disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7373","7420 Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Al-Asadi told us, he said: Ali bin Salih told us, on the authority of my father Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Shall I not teach you? Words, if you say them, you will be forgiven, even though you are forgiven: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Most Generous, there is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Great, Glory be to God. Lord of the seven heavens, and Lord of the Noble Throne, praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7374","7421 Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiya told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Musa, “We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So we landed in a valley on the ground, and the people raised their voices with the takbir, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O people! Be satisfied with yourselves. You do not call on a deaf person or an absent person. You call on a hearing person who is near. He said: And I was close to him: O Abdullah bin Qais, shall I not tell you a word from the treasure of Paradise? I said: Yes, he said: There is no power nor strength except in God. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7375","7422 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahhab, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, he said: “ We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a campaign, and we did not go up a hill or go down a valley without raising our voices with the takbir. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, approached us and said: “O people, give quarter to yourselves, for you will not leave a deaf person or an absent person. You call upon only the Hearer and the All-Seeer. Indeed, the one you call upon is closer to one of you than the neck of his camel. Then he said: O Abdullah bin Qais, shall I direct you to A word is one of the treasures of Paradise? There is no power nor strength except in God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7376","7423 Muhammad bin Hatim informed us, he said: I am Suwayd, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, He said: “We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a campaign, and he made us not go up a high place, nor go up a high place, nor go down a valley, except that he raised us up.” We raised our voices with takbeer, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us and said: “O people, be responsible for yourselves, for you are not Do you call upon a deaf person or an absent person? Rather, you call on a hearing and seeing person. Then he said: O Abdullah bin Qais, shall I not teach you a word that is part of a treasure in Paradise? There is no power nor strength except in God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7377","7424 Ahmad bin Nasr and Muhammad bin Aqeel told us, saying: Hafs told us, he said: Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray: O Living, O Sustaining One.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7378","7425 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas, he said: “It was part of the supplication of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And peace be upon him: that is, the Living, that is, the Ever-Subsisting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7379","7426 Uthman bin Abdullah told us, he said: Abu Muammar told me, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Husayn told me, he said: Abdul told me. Allah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “Oh God, I submit to you. And in You I have believed, and in You I have put my trust, and to You I turn, and in You I have contended. I seek refuge in Your Might, there is no god but You, lest you lead me astray. You are the Living Who does not You die, and the jinn and humans die.”"
"7380","7427 Yusuf bin Saeed informed us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika informed me, that he heard Muhammad Ibn Qays Ibn Makhrama, saying: I heard Aisha speaking. She said: Shall I not tell you about me and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I said: Yes, she said: “When my night had passed while he was with me, he put his sandals on his feet, put on his cloak, and spread the edge of his garment on his bed.” The hadith was narrated in its entirety. Ibn Wahb disagreed with him, so he narrated it on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, Suleiman bin Dawud informed us, saying: Abdullah bin Wahb told us, saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Many, that he heard Muhammad bin Qais say: I heard Aisha say: Shall I not tell you about the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? So he mentioned something similar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7381","7428 Ahmad bin Al-Azhar told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: I am Ibn Uyaynah, and Fudayl, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: Rabbi came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “When the Day of Resurrection comes, God will place the heavens on A finger, and the two lands are on a finger, and the mountains are on a finger. Fudayl said: And this and this and this and this and this, and the earth, and the water, And the rest of creation was like this. Then he shook them and said: Where are the kings? Indeed, the kingdom today belongs to God, the One, the Supreme. He said: Then the Messenger of God laughed. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him until his molars became visible, then he said: “And they have not estimated God as He deserves, while the earth as a whole has taken hold of Him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7382","7429 Omar bin Abdul Aziz told us, he said: Yusuf bin Adiy told us, he said: Otham told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, “When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, fell asleep, that is, turned over during the night, he said: There is no god but God, the One, the Subduer, the Lord of the heavens.” And the earth and what is between them, the Mighty, the Forgiving.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7383","7430 Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Abdullah bin Nafi’ Al-Zubayri told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Abi Hazim told me, on the authority of his father On the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The mighty man will take away his heavens.” And his earth is in his hand. He clenched his hands, and began to clench them and spread them out, then he said: I am the mighty, so where are the mighty, where are the arrogant? He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, leaned to his right and to his left, until I looked at the pulpit and part of it moved from underneath. I would even say: He is the one who has fallen because of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"7384","7431 And Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Anas said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “I will be the first of the people to have the ground split open from his skull on the Day of Resurrection, and there will be no pride. I will come to the gate of Paradise and hold its ring. He will say: Who is this? I will say: I am Muhammad. They will open for me and I will enter, and behold, the Almighty is facing me. So I prostrate to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7385","7432 Muhammad bin Uthman told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata’, on the authority of Amr bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Abu Bakr said: “O Messenger of God, teach me words that I can say in the morning and in the evening.” He said: Say: Oh God. Creator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself, and the evil of Satan and his trap. Say it. “In the morning, in the evening, and when you go to bed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7386","7433 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab informed me, on the authority of my father Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Suleiman bin Dawud informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, that Abu Hurairah used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God will grip the earth on the Day of Resurrection, and fold the heavens with His right hand, then He says: I am the king, where are the kings of the earth? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7387","7434 Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Aisha, she reported that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he used to say while bowing: “Glory be to the Holy One, Lord of the angels and the spirit.”"
"7388","7435 Ali bin Muslim told me, he said: Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith told me, he said: My father told me, he said: Hussein told me, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah said: Ibn Umar told me, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say when he came to bed: Praise be to God who He sufficed me and sheltered me, fed me and gave me drink, and He who bestowed favor upon me and bestowed upon me and gave me abundantly, praise be to God in every condition, O God, Lord of all things, And the King of all things, and the God of all things, I seek refuge in You from the Fire.”"
"7389","7436 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Maqsim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, read these verses one day on the pulpit: Appreciate God as he deserves, and the earth as a whole will be his grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be rolled up with his right hand, until the end of the verse. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace with his hands in this way. He seizes them and spreads them out, and sets the inside of them toward heaven. The Lord glorifies Himself: I am the mighty one. The King, I am the Mighty, I am the Generous, so the pulpit shook with him until we said: Let the pulpit fall down with him.”"
"7390","7437 Abu Dawud told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Maqsim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse: And they have not esteemed God according to His esteem.” And the entire earth will take him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said with his hand like this: He glorifies the Lord, and he described him. We have a chaste man who closes his hand and extends it. I am the mighty, I am the arrogant, I am the king, I am the Mighty, I am the Generous. So he shuddered at the Messenger. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the pulpit, so much so that we said: Let him prostrate himself in it."
"7391","7438 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, in his hadith, on the authority of Sufyan, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid informed us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Qaza’ah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: “Isolation was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Why Would any of you do that and did not say: “He should not do that,” for there is no created soul except Allah, its Creator.” The wording is attributed to Muhammad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7392","7439 Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, On the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, that he heard Abu Sarmah and Abu Sa`id al-Khudri say: “We captured captives in the battle of al-Mustaliq, which was The battle in which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, attacked Juwayriyah. There were some of us who wanted to take a family, and some of us wanted to He enjoys and sells, so we decided to isolate him, so we mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: You do not have to isolate yourself, for God has destined what is created until the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7393","7440 Ziyad bin Ayyub informed us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Ibn Asim, who is Amr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, Abu Bakr asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Order me some words to say in the morning and in the evening.” He said: Say: Oh God, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself and from the evil of Satan. He said “Say it in the morning, and in the evening, and when you go to bed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7394","7441 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Fudayl told us, on the authority of Sulaiman Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, God is peace, so when one of you sits, let him say: Greetings are to God and prayers and good things, peace be upon you.” O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God, I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, And I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then he chooses to speak whatever he wants.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7395","7442 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Khalaf told us, on the authority of Hafs bin Abdullah, on the authority of his uncle Anas, he said: “I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, a man was sitting and praying. When he knelt down, prostrated, and recited the tashahhud, he supplicated, and said in his supplication: O God, I ask you that praise be to you, no There is no god but You, the Most Benevolent, the Creator of the heavens and the earth, O Possessor of Majesty and Honour, O Ever-Living, O Sustaining One. Indeed, I ask You, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He greeted his companions: Do you know what he called upon? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, he called on the name of God Almighty. When he is called with it, he responds, and when asked with it, he gives.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7396","7443 Abu Bakr bin Hafs told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God is gentle and loves gentleness, and He gives more for gentleness than He does for violence.”"
"7397","7444 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan told us, and Abd al-A’la bin Wasil told us, He said: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Sulayman al-Ahwal, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made this supplication when he woke up at night: O God, praise be to You, You are the light of the heavens and the earth, and praise be to You, You are Sustainer of the heavens and the earth, and praise be to You, You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is in them. You are the Truth, and Your word is the Truth, and Your promise is the Truth. And meeting you is true, and Paradise is true, and Hell is true, and the prophets are true, and the Hour is true, O God, to you I have submitted, and in you I have believed, and upon you I put my trust, and to You I repent, and to You I dispute, and to You I judge, so forgive me what I have done forward and what I have delayed, and what I have concealed and what I have declared, You are God. There is no god but You\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"7398","7445 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. Whenever he stood up to pray in the middle of the night, he would say: O God, praise be to You, You are the light of the heavens and the earth, and to You belongs all praise. The establishment of the heavens and the earth, and praise be to You. You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is in them. You are the Truth, your word is the truth, and your promise is the truth. And meeting you is true, and Paradise is true, and Hell is true, and the Hour is true. Oh God, to You I have submitted, and in You I have believed, and in You I have put my trust, and to You I repent, and by you I dispute, and to you I judge, so forgive me what I have done before and what I have done in the future, and what I have pleased and what I have declared, you are my God, and there is no god but you.”"
"7399","7446 Muhammad bin Mansour informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: I heard Suleiman, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he got up to recite Hajj at night, he said: O God, praise be to You, You are the light of the heavens and the earth and whoever is in them, and praise be to You, You are the Sustainer of the heavens. And the earth and whoever is in them, and to You is praise. You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and whoever is in them. You are the truth, and your word is truth, and your promise is truth, and meeting you is true. True, and Paradise is true, and Hell is true, and the Hour is true, and the prophets are true, and Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, is true. Oh God, I submit to you. And in You I have believed, and in You I have put my trust, and to You I repent, and with You I have disputed, and to You I have judged, so forgive me what I have done forward and what I have delayed, and what I have pleased. And what I have declared, You are the advancer and You are the delayer, there is no god but You.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7400","7447 Ahmad bin Amr told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Urwa bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to him that she said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “O Messenger of God, Has there ever come to you a day more severe than the day of Uhud? He said: I have encountered some of your people, and the worst I have encountered among them was the day of Aqaba, when I came. I went to Ibn Abd Yalil bin Abd Kulal, but he did not answer me to what I wanted, so I set off with a worried expression on my face, and I did not wake up until By the horns of foxes, so I raised my head, and behold, a cloud had shaded me. I looked, and behold, therein was Gabriel, and he called me and said: Indeed, God is Almighty. God Almighty has heard what your people said to you, and what they responded to you, and he has sent to you the Angel of the Mountains so that you may order him whatever you wish regarding them. He said: Then the Angel of the Mountains called me. The mountains and he greeted me, then he said: O Muhammad, God has heard what your people said to you, and I am the king of the mountains, and your Lord has sent me to you. You may order me to do whatever you wish, if you wish, so that I may close upon them the two woods. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Rather, I hope that God will bring them out. “Among their descendants are those who worship God alone and do not associate anything with Him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7401","7448 Nasr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Ahmad told us, he said: Israel told us, and Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Musa, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, who is the son of Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, who is the son of Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me: “Indeed, I am the Sustainer, the Possessor of Power and the Firm.”"
"7402","7449 Amr ibn Ali informed us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa’id told us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ubayy Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Musa Al Ash’ari, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no one who is patient with harm he hears from God.” They pray for him to have a son, and he will heal them and provide for them.”"
"7403","7450 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Maqsim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said while he was on the pulpit: God takes His heavens and earth into His hands, then he says: I am God, and He holds between His fingers and spread them out, I am the Most Gracious, I am the King, until I looked at the pulpit, moving from the bottom of part of it, so much so that I could say: Is he a disgrace to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace?"
"7404","7451 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, then Al-Layth, that Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, that he said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Teach me a supplication that I may pray with in my prayers.” He said: Say: Oh God, I have wronged myself. “I have committed much injustice, and no one forgives sins except You, so forgive me with Your forgiveness, and have mercy on me, for You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.”"
"7405","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed and Abdul Rahman bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Marwan, he said: Yazid bin Kaysan told us, he said: Abu Hazim Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “There was a man from the Ansar with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with him was a boy of his, so he He brought it to him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do you have mercy on him? He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: God is more merciful to you than you are to him. And He is the Most Merciful of those who show mercy.” The word “Ubayd Allah” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7406","7452 Ismail bin Masoud told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Kahms, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him: “Have you seen that if I knew the Night of Decree, what would I say? He said: Say: O God, You are the Pardoner and You love to pardon, so pardon me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7407","7453 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Salem, On the authority of his father, he said: “The right hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was: ‘No,’ and he is the converter of hearts.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7408","Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Suhail, who said: Abu Salih used to “order us, if one of us wants to sleep, to lie down.” On his right side, then he says: Oh God, you are the Lord of the heavens, the Lord of the earth, the Lord of the Great Throne, our Lord and the Lord of everything, so give love By the nucleus, the revelation of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Qur’an, I seek refuge in You from the evil of everything, whose corner you take hold of. You are the first, so there is no one before you. One thing and you are the Last, there is nothing after you and you are the Manifest, there is nothing above you and you are the Hidden, there is nothing below you, settle the debt for us. “And enrich us from poverty.” He used to narrate that on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7409","7454 Muhammad ibn Bashar informed us, saying: Muhammad informed us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ya’la ibn Ata’, he said: I heard Amr ibn Asim, He heard Abu Hurairah say: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Tell me something that I should say when morning and when evening, he said: Say: O God, the Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, the Creator of the heavens and the earth, the Lord and Sovereign of all things, I bear witness that no There is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself, and the evil of Satan and his polytheism, in the morning, and in the evening, and when you go to bed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7410","Muhammad bin Issa informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Hassan, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Amir, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Adorn Him who is worthy of glory and honor.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7411","7456 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, you are peace, and from you is peace. Blessed are you, O Possessor of majesty and honor.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7412","7457 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: A successor, he is Ibn Khalifa, told us, on the authority of my nephew Anas, on the authority of Anas, he said: “I was sitting with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the episode, when a man came and greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace and to the people, and said: Peace be upon you, so he responded. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: May God’s peace, mercy, and blessings be upon you. He said: When the man sat down, he said: Praise be to God, many good thanks. Blessed in it, as our Lord loves and is pleased. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: How did he respond to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as he said? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, ten angels sought it out, all of them keen to write it down, but they did not manage. How do they write it? Until they were brought to Dhul-Izzah, and he said: Write it as My servant said. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7413","Al-Rabi’ bin Muhammad bin Issa informed us, on the authority of Adam bin Abi Iyas, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Hell will keep saying: Is there more? Until the Lord of Glory, Blessed and Most High, places his foot therein, and it will say: Never.” Never, by Your glory, and some of them are related to one another.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7414","7459 Ali bin Hajar told us, Ismail told us, he said: Musa bin Uqba told us, on the authority of Umm Khalid bint Khalid bin Saeed bin Al-Aas, She said: “I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, seeking refuge in God from the torment of the grave.”"
"7415","7460 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “It was He seeks refuge in God from the torment of the grave, and from the temptation of the Antichrist.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7416","7461 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu al-Zinad told us, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “Seek refuge in God from the temptation of the grave, and seek refuge in God from the temptation of life and death, seek refuge in God from the temptation of the Messiah.” Antichrist (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7417","7462 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, on the authority of Yahya, and Ibn Abi Adiy, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his bowing and prostration: Glory be to the Holy One, Lord of the angels and the spirit.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7418","7463 Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: I am Ismail, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifa, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah bin Ka’b, that Nafi’ bin Jubayr told him that Uthman ibn Abi Al-Aas “came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was overcome by pain that almost made him weak, so he mentioned That is for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Place your right hand where you complain. So wipe with it seven times, and say: I seek refuge in God’s glory and power from the evil I find, every time.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7419","7464 Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Abdul-Ala bin Hammad told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Hell will continue to be thrown into it, and it will say: Is there more? Until the Lord of the Worlds places His foot in it. Then some of them are connected to each other, and you say: May, may, by Your honor and generosity."
"7420","7465 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: Yazid and Abu Amir told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to seek refuge with Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein: “I seek refuge with you with the perfect words of God from all “A devil and a wild beast, and from every eye a mother.” And he says: This is how my father Abraham used to protect Ishmael and Isaac. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7421","7466 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Raja told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Uthman, who is Ibn al-Mughirah, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Jabir, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to present himself to people during the season, and he would say: Is there a man who will carry me to His people, for the Quraysh have prevented me from conveying the word of my Lord.”"
"7422","7467 Ubayd Allah bin Fadalah told us, he said: I am Suleiman bin Dawud, he said: Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The keys to the unseen are five: Indeed, God has knowledge of the Hour, and He will send down rain, and He knows what is in the wombs.” No soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware.”"
"7423","7468 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Al-Mawwal told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: “It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, teaches us istikharah in all matters, just as he teaches us a surah from the Qur’an,” and he cited the length of the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7424","7469 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God Almighty says: I am when My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he mentions Me. So if he mentions Me in Himself, I remember him to myself, and if he mentions me in a gathering, I remember him in a better gathering than him, and if he draws near to me an arm’s length, I draw near to him an arm’s length away. “And if he approaches me by an arm’s length, I will approach him a full length, and if he comes to me walking, I will come to him trotting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7425","7470 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: “When it was revealed: Say, He is the Powerful That He sends upon you a torment from above you. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I seek refuge in your face. He said: Or from under your feet. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I seek refuge in Your Face. He said: Or He will divide you into sects and make some of you taste the violence of one another. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “easier.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
